### Example API requests (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP client format)
### Demo tokens: demo-alice, demo-bob, demo-carol

### Health (no auth)
GET http://localhost:8000/api/v1/health

### Who am I
GET http://localhost:8000/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer demo-alice

### Chat — order lookup (tool route)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer demo-alice

{"message": "Where is my order ORD-1001?"}

### Chat — follow-up in the same session (replace the session_id)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer demo-alice

{"message": "Can I return it?", "session_id": "PASTE-SESSION-ID"}

### Chat — RAG policy question
POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer demo-bob

{"message": "What is your return policy for electronics?"}

### Create a session explicitly
POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer demo-alice

{"title": "Returns question"}

### List my sessions
GET http://localhost:8000/api/v1/sessions
Authorization: Bearer demo-alice

### Conversation history
GET http://localhost:8000/api/v1/sessions/PASTE-SESSION-ID/history
Authorization: Bearer demo-alice

### List allowlisted tools
GET http://localhost:8000/api/v1/tools

### Invoke a tool directly
POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/tools/invoke
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer demo-bob

{"tool": "check_return_eligibility", "arguments": {"order_id": "ORD-1004"}}

### Authorization check — Bob cannot read Alice's order (success=false)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/tools/invoke
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer demo-bob

{"tool": "lookup_order", "arguments": {"order_id": "ORD-1001"}}
